      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              POLITICAL ECONOMY OF MEDIA LANDSCAPE                |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  OWNERSHIP ANALYSIS          ADVERTISING LOGIC                   |\n|  -----------------           -----------------                   |\n|  Concentration               Audiences as product                |\n|  Conglomeration              Advertisers as real clients         |\n|  Horizontal/vertical         Content optimized for advertiser    |\n|  integration                 demographics, not public interest   |\n|                                                                  |\n|  PROPAGANDA MODEL            COMMODIFICATION                     |\n|  ----------------            ----------------                    |\n|  Herman & Chomsky (1988)     Commodification of information      |\n|  Five filters on news        Public goods as private goods       |\n|                              Enclosure of digital commons        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  KEY THEORISTS               REVENUE MODELS                      |\n|  =============               =============                       |\n|  Dallas Smythe               Advertising (legacy + digital)      |\n|  Graham Murdock              Subscription                        |\n|  Peter Golding               Public service                      |\n|  Vincent Mosco               Surveillance capitalism             |\n|  Herman & Chomsky            Data extraction                     |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
